T89 Linux e2e run at the final HEAD (review r12, after T85-T88), 2026-10-11
HEAD: b507f6a (feature/editor-ux), exported with `git archive b507f6a` (clean tree); this log and the T89 doc change are added afterwards (docs only)
Image: mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.63.0-noble (linux/arm64 on Docker Desktop, engine 29.8.1); @playwright/test 1.63.0
Node used for the runs: v22.23.3 (the T67/T71/T84 nodejs.org linux-arm64 tarball, re-checked against SHASUMS256.txt: OK, copied to /opt/node22,
  first on PATH; the image's own Node is not used). Inside the repo's engines (>=22.18 <23). pnpm 10.25.0 via corepack.
Docker CLI: static 27.3.1 aarch64 from download.docker.com (the T67 download).
How (the T84 harness, same prep.sh; full.sh only also keeps each run's raw output): repo copy in the container,
  `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, `pnpm exec prisma generate`, then plain `CI=1 pnpm test:e2e` (no --workers flag, so the config's 2 workers).
  Docker socket mounted from the host, TESTCONTAINERS_HOST_OVERRIDE=host.docker.internal (--add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway),
  TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_DISABLED=true (local only). The app server and its throwaway Postgres come from playwright.config.ts's webServer.
  .env = env.example with generated AUTH/CRON/LIMIT_KEY secrets and a dummy Sentry DSN; never the repo's .env databases.
  The host was kept awake with `caffeinate -i` for the whole run.

== What changed since T84 (6e46f69) ==
App: store/invoice-editor-store/save-command.ts (T85: a later save that leaves nothing unsaved takes the "kept for you to save" sentence off
  the issued notice). E2e: tests/e2e/editor-first-save-after-create.spec.ts:204 matches the line-only notice with exact: true (T88);
  tests/e2e/date-matrix.spec.ts creates the UTC-10 custom price at 00:30Z (T86).

